---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "The Geriatrician's Guide — Senior Living Guidance from a Stanford-Trained Geriatrician";
const description = "Clinical clarity for families facing senior living decisions. Free tools, physician-written guidance, and no placement commissions. Ever.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>

  <!-- SECTION 2 — HERO -->
  <section class="hero" data-screen-label="Hero">
    <div class="hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__text">
        <h1>Clear guidance for the decisions that matter most.</h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">Geriatrics is the field that asks what matters to you. I trained in it at Stanford, then spent years caring for older adults in their homes and across senior living communities. I built this for the same reason I chose the field: to be useful in the ways that actually matter.</p>
        <div class="hero__cta">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--gold hero__cta-label">Free resources</p>
          <a class="btn btn--accent" href="/is-it-time">Take the Is It Time? assessment
            <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/tour-kit">Get the Tour Day Kit
            <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero__figure">
        <div class="hero__media">
          <img src="/images/hero-genualdi.png" alt="Dr. Michael Genualdi, MD, board-certified geriatrician" width="1264" height="848" />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="hero__caption">Michael Genualdi, MD<br><span class="hero__caption-sub">Founder, The Geriatrician&rsquo;s Guide</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2.5 — ROADMAP STRIP -->
  <section class="roadmap" data-screen-label="Roadmap">
    <div class="roadmap__inner">
      <span class="roadmap__step"><a href="/is-it-time">Is it time?</a></span>
      <span class="roadmap__sep">&mdash;</span>
      <span class="roadmap__step"><a href="/starting-the-conversation">Start the conversation</a></span>
      <span class="roadmap__sep">&mdash;</span>
      <span class="roadmap__step"><a href="/tour-kit">Tour communities</a></span>
      <span class="roadmap__sep">&mdash;</span>
      <span class="roadmap__step"><a href="/the-long-road">Plan the road ahead</a></span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3 — AUTHORITY BRIDGE -->
  <section class="authority" data-screen-label="Authority bridge">
    <div class="authority__inner">
      <p>Most physicians have never set foot inside a senior living community. I spent years visiting dozens of them &mdash; meeting with the nurses and directors responsible for what actually happened to residents between my visits, reviewing medication lists, learning the prescribing and pharmacy processes well enough to know exactly where they fail. I know what a well-run community looks like from the inside. This is what I built so you can too.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4 — LEAD MAGNET TEASER (capture form lives on /tour-kit; one pipeline, no duplicate ESP) -->
  <section class="lead-light" data-screen-label="Lead magnet">
    <div class="lead-light__inner">
      <p class="lead-light__eyebrow">Free Download</p>
      <h2 class="lead-light__headline">The Tour Day Kit</h2>
      <p class="lead-light__sub">Four printable tools for the day you tour &mdash; the Checklist, the Card, the Notes sheet, and the Community Scorecard. The questions a geriatrician asks, in your pocket.</p>

      <div class="proof-row">
        <div class="proof-item">
          <h3>Before you arrive</h3>
          <p>The Checklist &mdash; every domain to look up, prepare, and ask about before you schedule anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item">
          <h3>On the tour</h3>
          <p>The Card and Notes sheet &mdash; the questions in your pocket, and somewhere to capture each visit before they blur together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item">
          <h3>After you leave</h3>
          <p>The Community Scorecard &mdash; a clean way to score each community and lay your finalists side by side.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/tour-kit">Get the free Tour Day Kit
        <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5 — INDEPENDENCE TRUST BLOCK -->
  <section class="independence" data-screen-label="Independence">
    <div class="independence__inner">
      <div class="independence__rule"></div>
      <p class="independence__quote">No placement commissions. No facility money. Ever.</p>
      <p class="independence__body">I built this because people navigating this decision deserve at least one voice that has nothing to gain from where their loved one ends up.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6 — PRODUCT TEASER -->
  <section class="teaser" data-screen-label="Product teaser">
    <div class="teaser__inner">
      <div class="teaser__text">
        <p class="teaser__eyebrow">The Flagship</p>
        <h2 class="teaser__title">The Long Road</h2>
        <p class="teaser__sub">A Geriatrician&rsquo;s Complete Guide to Senior Care Decisions</p>
        <p class="teaser__body">A 247-page reference covering the full arc &mdash; from the first signs of decline through end-of-life decisions. The finances, the tour, the contract, the conversation you&rsquo;ve been avoiding. Written for anyone navigating this for someone they love.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/the-long-road">Learn more
          <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="teaser__figure">
        <img src="/images/the-long-road-cover.png" alt="The Long Road — A Geriatrician's Complete Guide to Senior Care Decisions, by Michael D. Genualdi, MD" width="2474" height="3200" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7 — BLOG TEASER -->
  <section class="blog-teaser" data-screen-label="Blog teaser">
    <div class="blog-teaser__inner">
      <p class="blog-teaser__eyebrow">From the Guide</p>
      <h2 class="blog-teaser__title">Recent articles</h2>
      <p class="blog-teaser__intro">Physician-written notes on the questions that come up most on tours, in contracts, and in the room with your loved one.</p>
      <div class="blog-teaser__grid">
        <article class="blog-teaser__card">
          <a class="blog-teaser__card-title" href="/blog/assisted-living-contract-questions">Five Questions to Ask Before Signing an Assisted Living Contract</a>
          <p class="blog-teaser__card-meta">July 7, 2026</p>
          <p class="blog-teaser__card-desc">Most families sign assisted living contracts without reading the arbitration clause. Here is what a geriatrician looks for before a family puts pen to paper.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="blog-teaser__card">
          <a class="blog-teaser__card-title" href="/blog/memory-care-staffing-question">The One Staffing Question Nobody Asks on a Memory Care Tour</a>
          <p class="blog-teaser__card-meta">June 23, 2026</p>
          <p class="blog-teaser__card-desc">What is posted on the wall and what is staffed at 11 PM on a Tuesday are two different numbers. A geriatrician explains how to get the real one.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <a class="textlink" href="/blog">Read all articles
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
</content>
